    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n`HarmonyBrowserTool` previously hardcoded `ExaBackend`. This adds a `BROWSER_BACKEND` env var (defaults to `\"youcom\"`) that lets users select between `YouComBackend` and `ExaBackend`.\r\n\r\nThis mirrors the pattern already used in gpt-oss, which defaults to `\"youcom\"` in all three of its entry points:\r\n\r\n- [`browser_server.py`](https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/gpt-oss-mcp-server/browser_server.py) (MCP server): `os.getenv(\"BROWSER_BACKEND\", \"youcom\")`\r\n- [`chat.py`](https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/gpt_oss/chat.py) (CLI chat): `os.getenv(\"BROWSER_BACKEND\", \"youcom\")`\r\n- [`reference-system-prompt.py`](https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss/blob/main/gpt-oss-mcp-server/reference-system-prompt.py) (reference setup): `os.getenv(\"BROWSER_BACKEND\", \"youcom\")`\r\n\r\nvLLM's demo tool server uses gpt-oss's backend library. Defaulting to `\"youcom\"` aligns with the upstream project's existing choice. Users who need Exa can set `BROWSER_BACKEND=exa`.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Read `BROWSER_BACKEND` env var in `HarmonyBrowserTool.__init__` (defaults to `\"youcom\"`, matching gpt-oss)\r\n- Select `YouComBackend` (with `YDC_API_KEY`) or `ExaBackend` (with `EXA_API_KEY`) based on the env var\r\n- Warning message includes the relevant env var name (`YDC_API_KEY` or `EXA_API_KEY`)\r\n\r\n## Non-duplication\r\n\r\nSearched for existing PRs matching `BROWSER_BACKEND`, `HarmonyBrowserTool`, and `YouComBackend` in this repo. No open or closed PRs found.\r\n\r\n## Test commands\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython3 -c \"import ast; ast.parse(open(\\\"vllm/entrypoints/mcp/tool.py\\\").read())\"\r\n# Result: OK, file parses cleanly\r\n\r\nawk 'length > 88 {print NR}: {length} chars' vllm/entrypoints/mcp/tool.py\r\n# Result: no lines over 88 chars\r\n```",
